Java Libraries are the collection of pre-defined classes and interfaces which consists of different variables and methods. 
These methods have a definite function which is used in the java programs. 
Some popular java libraries are java.lang, java.io, 
java.lang is a special library because this library is automatically imported in all the classes or interfaces or any program we create in java.
In the java.lang there is a special class called the Object class. The feature of this class is this class is known as the supermost class of java. This is the
super class of all the java classes. In other words, all the classes/interfaces created in java will automatically inherit this class and all its methods.

Some important methods of this class are, 
toString()
hachCode()
equals()
